Current files are still in beta and subject to change.


This project uses modified and stock files from various creators and projects. As so I will include links to stock files for you finding and a brief description if needed.
  
  Z-MOD - Original creator is CovertPluto3502s project I got from Printables https://www.printables.com/model/475994-ender-5-triple-z-e5tz-v2
    I have modified it to use the hardware I had on hand and to use couplers from an ender 3. I would however recommend using all of the original files as the couplers he used
    are objectively better.

  ELECTRONICS/Enclosure - For the skirt I used the Mercury one.1 electronics skirt with stock feet. I did not have access to din rail mounts so I modified the Mercury one.1
    din rail mounts to work with 2020 extrusions. This is how I mounted all of my electronics.
    As for the Electronics themselves I used 1 BTT SKR MINI E3 v3, 1 creality 4.2.7 mainboard, and a BTT PI. All of this is running off of the stock meanwell 350 watt PSU
    For the CPAP setup I used WS 4070 and used a mount I found on Thangs.com (dont remember which one but its just a prefference thing so look at some and decide which to use)

  X/Y - 4 350mm MGN12H rails and 2 400mm MGN9H rails I purchases them from CNA store on aliexpress.
  
  TOOLHEAD - (I would reccomend printing all toolhead parts in as redgit material as you can, I am using PETCF) This toolhead is designed for the Trangle Labs DragonAce hotend 
    with MZE(Melt Zone Extender). It should work with any hotend of the same length with rapido mounting holes. As for the extruder it is using a Mirrored Sherpa Micro by          ANNEX Engineering https://github.com/Annex-Engineering/Sherpa_Micro-Extruder (Ensure you mirror files in the slicer).
